# Perft for all 960 Chess960 start positions, sealed from an independent
# engine. Regenerate with:
#   python tools/chess960diff.py seal-startpos tests/perft/chess960-startpos.epd \
#       -depth 4,5 -oracle <uci engine>
#
# One line per Scharnagl SP number, in order, so the Nth position line is
# SP N-1. Every castling geometry Chess960 can produce appears here at least
# once, which is what makes this the broad net; tests/perft/chess960.epd is
# the sharp one. Two depths so the fast gate can cap at the shallower:
#   make perft       depth 4, seconds
#   make perft-all   both, minutes
#
# SP 518 is the standard array, and its counts must equal the standard start
# position's in tests/perft/standard.epd. The two suites reach the same board
# down completely different code paths - one parses KQkq into fixed squares,
# the other derives the array from an index and spells its rights HAha - so
# agreeing there is worth more than either count alone.
#
# This file also pins the SP NUMBERING. board.c derives the array from the
# index; if that derivation drifted by even one position, these FENs would
# stop being the ones `chess960 selftest` generates, and it says so.
bbqnnrkr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/BBQNNRKR w HFhf - 0 1 ;D4 201143 ;D5 4975808
bqnbnrkr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/BQNBNRKR w HFhf - 0 1 ;D4 198393 ;D5 4863733
